4. Combined metrics (e.g., RADIUS_RATIO, ELONGATEDNESS, HOLLOWS_RATIO) - these encode relationships between radii, area, and bounding polygons, differentiating vehicles with large or complex hollows (e.g., cars vs. buses).

Features involving interactions or transformations (e.g., divide, multiply, log) among these core groups may further uncover discriminative properties. Shape-specific metrics like elongation or scattering likely dominate distinctions across categories.

